WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is
an Emmy Award-winning acto

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from his work
on "Will &amp; Grace"

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.837 line:92%
and "American Horror Story."

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:07.374
He stars in "Call Me Kat," which
airs Thursday nights on Fox.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Leslie Jordan.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.177 size:75% position:38% line:92%
How are you, Leslie?

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good!
Thank you for having me.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I hope I'm righ
in saying this.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like a very good time
to be Leslie Jordan.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I don't know.
Give me a good pandemic,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I seem to flourish,
which is an awful thing to say

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:32.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just have done so well
during this time

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's amazing
what I've accomplished.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things you did
was you found your way

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
onto Instagram,
and you provided a lot of jo

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.875 size:84% position:42%
and comfort to people
who were looking for it

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
during this
really troubling time.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you know, I really didn't
set out to do that.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was stuck in Tennessee
at my mom's house --

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.386
my mama, my sweet mama --
and I was going crazy.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.690
And I had -- I had not bee
on Instagram for a while.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.461 size:84% position:42%
I mean, about a year --
about two years ago,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was on a TV show called
"The Cool Kids,"

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.600
and the head of publicity
at the time would tell me,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.603
"Post, you know, that funn
thing you said, post this.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.939
And I thought, I didn't know
what she was talking about

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really didn't.
I thought maybe she meant

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
post-its,
those little yellow things

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, she said, "No, you nee
to put that on Instagram."

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she looked at me,
and she said,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You don't have an Instagram
account, do you?"

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.484 line:92%
I said, "No, ma'am, I don't.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so they opened me one,
and within a week,

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.623
I had 20,000 followers,
and I couldn't shut up about it.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.458 line:92%
I said, "Can you believe?"

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "That's nothing
compared to what you can have.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, Megan Mullally
from "Will &amp; Grace" posted -

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:42.735
reposted something of mine
I jumped to 80,000 followers

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.337 line:92%
and i couldn't believe it.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when the --
when the stay-at-home orders

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.010 size:78% position:39%
happened and I didn't
have anything to do,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in Tennessee,
I started posting twice a day,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
just silliness,
just silly stuff.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my friend called
from California.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.455 line:92%
He said, "You've gone viral.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "No, honey,
I'm in Tennessee with my mama.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm fine.
I don't have COVID."

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "No! You've gone vira
on the Internet."

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:14.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, here we go.
I don't know, 5.6 million.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have no idea.
I just, you know --

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
It's well-deserved.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.772
You mentioned being in Tennessee
with your mom

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your twin sisters, as well
correct?

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I have
identical twin sisters

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are 22 months
younger than me.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.549 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And they live with mom.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like
a dog and pony show.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
I bought them
a really pretty house,

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best thing
I ever did as an adult.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
Looks like Laura Ashley
threw up in there.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But it's just precious.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:43.363
And I get back there quite a bit
to see mama and them,

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we say in the South.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are they happy to see you
when you come home?

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, they are.
You know what?

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we were growing up, m
sisters got all the attention.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:54.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think
that's what's wrong with me.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Both laugh ]
Because identical twins

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
and mother back then, you know
in the '50s and '60s,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.448
would put them in little outfits
that matched,

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people would
"Ooh" and "Ahh,"

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'd be over there pullin
out my pee-pee

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:09.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
and turning cartwheels,
whatever I could think of!

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:12.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Somebody, please,
look at me, look at me!"

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...
-Now, Leslie,

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:17.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
you first made your way --
was it directly from Tennessee

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Los Angeles in the '80s
-I did.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:25.271 size:84% position:42%
I took a Greyhound bus.
I had -- It was 1982.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mother sewed $1,200
that I had saved waiting table

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
into my underpants.
And I got --

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:36.049 size:84% position:42%
I got off at the corner
of De Longpre and Vine,

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a block below
Hollywood and Vine,

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:43.356
which is the story of my lif
and my career, one block below

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But -- And I just --

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I don't know.
I don't know how it happened

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just happened.
You know, I just hit town

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a time when there was a lad
named Clara Peller

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:58.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of Chicago
on a Wendy's commercial.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "Where's the beef?
And all of a sudden,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
they all wanted,
you know, character actors

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I started doing commercial
and this and that.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I got
on "Murphy Brown,"

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.951
and I'll give you my whole
résumé, if you want me to,

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you ask.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:17.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, are you happy to be bac
on a sitcom now?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.427 size:75% position:38%
-This one, you know,
I told Mayim Bialik

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.629 size:75% position:38%
when I first started
working on the show,

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:26.532
I said, "You know, this is
the best show I've been on."

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.133 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She said, "Oh."

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.403 size:84% position:42%
I said, "No, I'm having
more fun right now."

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:33.039
I don't know if it's 'caus
I'm 65 and I've done it all,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:36.309
you know, and now I'm just ready
to have a good time,

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.810 line:92%
but it's so beautifully written.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
Darlene Hunt, that created it,
I play a character

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:45.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's so close to me,
I'm not even really acting

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.120 size:88% position:44%
I thought the other day,
"Why is this so easy?"

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought,
"'Cause you're just out there,

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:52.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, being yourself."
And we have such a great cast,

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have a really,
really good time.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:59.432
And I think it comes through
I hope it just runs forever.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:02.168 size:84% position:42%
-Another exciting thing
you have coming up is,

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.569 line:92%
you're writing a book of essays.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
This won't be
your first book, though.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.206 line:92%
How did the previous efforts go?

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:11.577
-Well, my last book was called
"My Trip Down the Pink Carpet,

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had some axes to grind
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.249 size:81% position:41%
You know, I was raised
in the Baptist church,

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:20.453 line:92%
and I've been baptized 14 times.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:21.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every time
the preacher would say,

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Would the live sinner
come forward?" I'd go forward.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "I believe I baptized
you this summer."

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"Well, I don't think it took."

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had some axes to grind.
So, I wrote --

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:37.103
This time, I just thought,
"I'm gonna just sit down

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:40.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
and write some funny stories
about little lessons

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.708 line:92%
I've learned along the way."

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm so tickled with the wa
it turned out,

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the publishers
are over the moon with it.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's gonna come ou
on Mother's Day,

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:51.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a wonderful tribute
to my mother.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.486 size:75% position:38%
So, it's a good time
to be Leslie Jordan.

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:54.954 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's just a good time.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:58.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also --
You used to do one-man shows

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would do a fair amount
a year.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ooh!
I'd do 45 venues a year.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:07.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
I trotted from one end
of this country to the other

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would tell,
you know, funny stories.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was the only one
really doing what I was doin

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the time,
because what I would do is

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.642 size:84% position:42%
I would go to gay bars,
usually, and tell them,

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Listen, you take the --
you take the bar.

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll get them all in here,
and I'll take the gate.

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.015 line:92%
We'll charge them 20 bucks."

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'd do some horse trading
and I'd walk away

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.853 line:92%
with $4,000, $5,000 in a night

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:32.392
And so, I just went, you know,
gay bar to gay bar to gay ba

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.926 size:78% position:39% line:92%
doing that for years.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.996
Oh, gosh.
I don't have to do that anymore.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got a few dollars
in the bank now.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:39.632 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I don't have to do that.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:42.034
-Well, I'm sorry I missed
my opportunity to see it.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:45.238
It must've been something, but I
can't wait to read your book

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, Leslie,
please do come back soon.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
This has been
an absolute delight.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:52.779
-I would love to.
Thank you so much for having me.

